35,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, my suspicions were right. The room usage is totally unbalanced, and the cleaning is a nightmare. One person has been doing all the heavy lifting while others just leave their stuff to rot.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The soundproofing is nonexistent; you can hear everything through the wall. Also, people are eating at their desks, leaving crumbs in keyboards and filling the bins daily. The current situation is messy and lacks privacy.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are paying a significant amount for external rooms for very small groups. Furthermore, the current empty room requires no maintenance, suggesting that adding complex equipment may increase our burden on facilities.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, the numbers are actually pretty big! We spent 68,000 yen on outside rooms last year! And the fit-outs cost either 96,000 or 141,000 yen. That's a lot of money to think about!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"It's even worse than I thought. We've barely any space for unplanned chats, and the last time something awkward happened, it was right in front of everyone. We really need a private place to actually talk.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, if people are already eating at their desks and making a mess, maybe we should just give them a proper place to do it? But @May, I'm worried about who will actually clean it.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, giving them a proper place might stop the crumbs at the desks, but it doesn't solve the noise. If we have a kitchen, the sound of cooking and chatting will still leak through that thin wall.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, your findings regarding the lack of private space for difficult conversations are poignant. If we continue to pay for external rooms for small groups, we are merely exporting our needs rather than solving them.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, you're right! Why pay for a room on the main road when we have one right here? But the fit-out costs are so high! We have to be really careful about which one we pick!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, the cost is high, but how much is it worth to actually feel comfortable with each other? If we keep ignoring the human side, we're just paying for a room we can't even use properly.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, I agree that the human side matters, but the ""human side"" is exactly why I'm worried. If we just make it a social space without a system, the same few people will end up cleaning everyone else's mess.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, that's why a structured use is better. If we choose a meeting space, we have a calendar and clear rules. A kitchen or a lounge just invites the same chaos and noise we already have.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must consider the long-term cost of our time. If we choose a path that requires constant, uncoordinated upkeep, we are simply trading financial expense for human exhaustion. A sustainable system is the only true economy.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Misaki, a calendar sounds like a great way to keep things fair! But @Servas, if we spend 141,000 yen on a meeting room, is that better than paying for outside rooms every year? I want to save money!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, if we spend that money once, we stop paying the 68,000 yen every year! But more importantly, we stop having awkward talks in front of everyone. We need a place where we can actually be a team.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"I see your point, @Kenji, but a meeting room doesn't stop the crumbs at the desks that @Misaki mentioned. If we don't address the eating habits, we're just ignoring one problem to solve another.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"Actually, a meeting room is for work, not food. If we designate it as such, it reinforces that eating belongs in a kitchen or away from the desks, rather than encouraging more mess in the office.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,It is wise to seek a solution that addresses both the financial drain and the emotional toll. A dedicated space for focused interaction would eliminate external costs and protect our collective peace of mind.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'm starting to think a meeting room is the smartest! It stops the money from leaking out to that other place, and a calendar makes it fair for everyone. Let's pick the one that saves us the most!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm glad we're agreeing! A meeting space solves the privacy issue, stops the external spending, and gives us a dedicated spot to actually connect. It's the best way to fix our team's atmosphere.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
